# Requests for the API while it runs locally (`dotnet run --project src/NpAspire.AppHost`).
# Variable names must not contain dots: Rider's HTTP client can't resolve them.
@apiHost = http://localhost:5104

### Health: all checks (Development only)
GET {{apiHost}}/health
Accept: text/plain

### Liveness: checks tagged "live" (Development only)
GET {{apiHost}}/alive
Accept: text/plain

### OpenAPI document (Development only)
GET {{apiHost}}/openapi/v1.json
Accept: application/json

### Status check: overall health (data: 0 Unhealthy, 1 Degraded, 2 Healthy); 503 when unhealthy. No token needed.
GET {{apiHost}}/api/v1/diagnostics
Accept: application/json

### Auth check: 200 with a token granting read:profile; 401 without a usable token, 403 without a role.
# Rider: put the token in http-client.private.env.json (gitignored) next to this file:
#   { "dev": { "accessToken": "<access token>" } }
# and run the request with the "dev" environment selected.
GET {{apiHost}}/api/v1/auth/check
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
